n        for fn in files:\n            s_file = pathlib.Path(root) / fn\n            d_file = target_dir / fn\n            copy_and_verify_file(s_file, d_file, manifest)\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\nmanifest = []\n\n<truncated 10662 bytes>\nnscript.jsonl`, `transcript_full.jsonl`, steps, tasks, and `scratch/`.\n- `antigravity/annotations/{CONV_ID}.pbtxt` & `antigravity/chapter_titles/{CONV_ID}.pb`.\n- `summary_extract.db` — Isolated `conversation_summaries` row + `conversations_fts` search rows (merges safely without overwriting existing chats).\n- `workspace/Exploit/` — Complete snapshot of the `Exploit` project directory.\n- `manifest.sha256.json` — SHA-256 and byte-size verification manifest for all bundled files.\n- `import_conversation.py` — Automated importer with pre-import checksum verification, safe SQLite merge, and post-import integrity check.\n\n## Instructions When Booted Into Drive `S:` (Wait: `S:` may be `C:` when booted!)\n1. Copy `workspace\\\\Exploit` to your Desktop (for example `C:\\\\Users\\\\Admin\\\\Desktop\\\\Exploit`) if you also want the project files locally.\n2. Tell the AI inside Antigravity (or run in terminal after closing Antigravity briefly so `conversation_summaries.db` isn't locked):\n   ```powershell\n   python \"<path-to-bundle>\\\\import_conversation.py\" --workspace \"C:\\\\Users\\\\Admin\\\\Desktop\\\\Exploit\"\n   ```\n   *(If you give this to the AI while Antigravity is running, have the AI copy `conversations/`, `brain/`, `annotations/`, `chapter_titles/` and run the merge, or close/reopen Antigravity right after so the sidebar refreshes `conversation_summaries.db`.)*\n\"\"\"\n(DEST / 'IMPORT_INSTRUCTIONS.md').write_text(instructions, encoding='utf-8')\n\n(DEST / 'manifest.sha256.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2), encoding='utf-8')\nprint(f'TOTAL exported & verified manifest files: {len(manifest)}')\n'@ | C:\\Python314\\python.exe -\nTask logs are available at: file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/.gemini