nt to the exact technologies, components, and problems involved before finalizing implementation decisions. Cross-reference the research with the existing implementation to identify\n<truncated 2550 bytes>\nf neither root access nor relevant Custom ROM functions are available, use standard ADB capabilities. You can even force stop/kill the app, Clear Logs at system or at kernel level if you want to see the issues further, basically anything you need to purge whatever issue it is.\r\n14: 12. **CRITICAL/SYSTEM FILE & LOG BACKUP:** When modifying, replacing, or deleting any system or critical OS file (local or on-device via ADB/root), create a timestamped backup directory at `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\` and follow this exact two-stage sequence:\r\n15:    - **Pre-Modification Target File Backup (BEFORE touching live files):**\r\n16:      - *Local Files:* Copy the untouched original file(s) into `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\files\\`, preserving the full relative directory structure to prevent filename collisions.\r\n17:      - *Android/ADB Files (under Rule 11):* Create an on-device backup in the same directory (`cp -a <file> <file>.bak`) to preserve exact UID/GID ownership, permissions, and SELinux contexts (`ls -Z`), AND pull a copy with its recorded `stat`/`ls -lZ` metadata to `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\files\\`.\r\n18:      - *Verification:* Verify that the target file backups exist and have a non-zero byte size matching the originals before modifying live system files. If the backup fails, abort immediately.\r\n19:    - **Post-Implementation Log Archival (ONLY AFTER executing the `implementation_plan.md` successfully):** Do not pre-backup session logs or plans. Once the implementation is completed and verified, copy the final `implementation_plan.md` and `.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl` in full from the active session directory (`C:\\Users\\Admin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\<ACTIVE_SESSION_ID>\\`) into the same `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>